  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0461' contains 6 tables. The tables are described as follows:\n1. **Product**: This table holds information about the products. The columns include Category (a string), Description (a string), Location (a string), Name (a string), Product_ID (an integer, primary key), Stock_Quantity (an integer), Unit_Price (a float), and Unit_of_Measurement (a string).\n2. **Delivery_Personnel**: This table contains information about the delivery personnel. The columns include Delivery_Personnel_ID (an integer, primary key), Gender (a boolean), Name (a string), Phone (a string), and Position (a string).\n3. **Customer**: This table contains information about the customers. The columns include Address (a string), Age (an integer), Customer_ID (an integer, primary key), Gender (a boolean), Name (a string), and Phone (a string).\n4. **Order**: This table holds information about the orders. The columns include Customer_ID (an integer, foreign key referencing Customer), Delivery_Address (a string), Order_Creation_Time (a datetime), Order_Number (an integer, primary key), Order_Status (a string), and Total_Order_Price (a float).\n5. **Order_Product**: This table maps the products in an order to the orders. The columns include Order_ID (an integer, foreign key referencing Order) and Product_ID (an integer, foreign key referencing Product), along with Product_Quantity (an integer). Both Order_ID and Product_ID form the primary key of this table.\n6. **Order_Delivery**: This table maps the delivery personnel to the orders. The columns include Delivery_Personnel_ID (an integer, foreign key referencing Delivery_Personnel), Estimated_Delivery_Time (a datetime), and Order_ID (an integer, foreign key referencing Order). Both Order_ID and Delivery_Personnel_ID form the primary key of this table.\nThis schema is designed to maintain a detailed record of product orders, their quantities, delivery personnel, and associated information. It ensures referential integrity by linking all the tables together through foreign keys.",
  "gold_question": "The system is a product distribution center information management system. In terms of product management, the system maintains detailed information for each product, including Product ID, Name, Unit Price, Stock Quantity, Unit of Measurement, Category, Description, and Storage Location. In terms of distribution personnel management, the system records basic information for each distribution personnel, including Delivery Personnel ID, Name, Phone, Gender, and Position, to facilitate personnel scheduling. In terms of customer management, the system maintains basic information for customers, including Customer ID, Name, Gender, Age, Phone, and Address, ensuring accurate processing and delivery of orders. In terms of order management, the system records complete information for each order, including Customer ID, Product ID, Order Creation Time, Product Quantity, Total Order Price, Delivery Address, Order Status, Estimated Delivery Time, and Responsible Delivery Personnel ID, enabling comprehensive tracking and management of the order process. Through the collaborative operation of these functional modules, the system achieves precise management of product inventory, automation of order processing, and real-time monitoring of the delivery process.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0461.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0461\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stock_quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `unit_price` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `unit_of_measurement` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `delivery_personnel` (\n  `delivery_personnel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` boolean DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`delivery_personnel_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` boolean DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order` (\n  `order_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `delivery_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `order_creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_order_price` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_product` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`, `product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `order` (`order_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_product_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_delivery` (\n  `delivery_personnel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `estimated_delivery_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`delivery_personnel_id`, `order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_delivery_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`delivery_personnel_id`) REFERENCES `delivery_personnel` (`delivery_personnel_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_delivery_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `order` (`order_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
